<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<nav class="navbar">
  <a href="/">← Home</a>
  <strong>📝 POST Form Demo</strong>
</nav>
<div class="container">
  <div class="card">
    <h2>📝 HTML Form – POST Request Handling</h2>
    <p>Fill in the form and submit. Express reads <code>req.body</code> using <code>express.urlencoded()</code> middleware.</p>

    <% if (error) { %>
      <div class="alert-error" style="margin-bottom:16px;">❌ <%= error %></div>
    <% } %>
    <% if (result) { %>
      <div class="alert-success" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        ✅ <strong>Form submitted successfully!</strong><br>
        Name: <strong><%= result.name %></strong> |
        Email: <strong><%= result.email %></strong> |
        Age: <strong><%= result.age %></strong> |
        Course: <strong><%= result.course %></strong><br>
        <small>Submitted at: <%= result.submittedAt %></small>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <form action="/form" method="POST">
      <label for="name"><strong>Name *</strong></label>
      <input type="text" id="name" name="name" placeholder="Your full name" required>

      <label for="email"><strong>Email *</strong></label>
      <input type="email" id="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required>

      <label for="age"><strong>Age</strong></label>
      <input type="number" id="age" name="age" placeholder="e.g. 21" min="1" max="100">

      <label for="course"><strong>Course</strong></label>
      <select id="course" name="course">
        <option value="">-- Select Course --</option>
        <option value="Backend Development">Backend Development</option>
        <option value="Full Stack">Full Stack</option>
        <option value="Data Science">Data Science</option>
      </select>

      <button type="submit" class="btn">Submit Form</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>💡 How POST Works in Express</h2>
    <pre>
// Middleware to parse form data
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));

// POST route
app.post('/form', (req, res) => {
  const { name, email, age, course } = req.body;
  // validate and respond...
});
    </pre>
  </div>
</div>
<footer>&copy; 2026 Satyam Koranga – Exp 12</footer>
</body>
</html>
